 summary="The committee invited the Department of Children and Youth to give information. There are 77 reception centres (children and family shelters) and welfare homes for long-term care; in 2569 there are 8,198 Thai children and 408 foreign children in care. Children involved in births registered with a false father are protected under the Child Protection Act B.E. 2546 (2003) with multidisciplinary teams while the steps to revoke nationality are completed before they return to their home country. The department suggested making the birth registration process stricter, starting from antenatal care. The committee also appointed honorary advisers and members of the subcommittee on older persons, set how to study preventing kratom drinks mixed with other substances, and prepared 2 field visits, including Pathum Thani (26 Aug 2569).",
